## Bluetooth method
8 s `bluetoothctl --timeout 8 scan on`; at 6 s, `bluetoothctl info` for each listed device, reading RSSI (decimal in parentheses).
A device counts in b_n if it shows in this scan's [NEW]/[CHG] Device lines or has an RSSI during discovery. BlueZ clears RSSI when discovery stops,
and unpaired devices expire about 30 s after (they carry over into the next scan, but are not counted unless seen again). Addresses stay in pipe memory only and are dropped.
